.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt CLOCK 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm clock ,
.Nm times ,
.Nm clock_settime ,
.Nm clock_getcpuclockid ,
.Nm adjtime
.Nd process and system time
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In time.h
.Ft clock_t
.Fn clock void
.Ft clock_t
.Fn times "struct tms *buffer"
.Ft int
.Fn clock_settime "clockid_t clock" "const struct timespec *value"
.Ft int
.Fn clock_getcpuclockid "pid_t pid" "clockid_t *clock"
.Ft int
.Fn adjtime "const struct timeval *delta" "struct timeval *olddelta"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These interfaces read or adjust process and system clocks. .Fn clock reports consumed CPU
time; .Fn times fills the process-time structure; the clock_* functions operate on a clock id.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn clock returns the CPU time or -1. .Fn times returns the elapsed clock or -1. The remaining
functions return 0 or -1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EINVAL is returned for an unknown clock id. .Er EPERM is returned for a clock that cannot
be set.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clock_gettime 2 ,
.Xr libc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn clock returns -1 and .Fn times fails until CPU accounting exists. .Fn clock_settime
returns .Er EPERM.
See C44 and A-time-14.
